# Theming and tokens

- Raw hex colours live only in `tokens.css` (defaults) and `themes.css` (era themes).
  Components use `var(--color-gx-*)` and derive shades with `color-mix(in oklab, ...)`.
  `check-css.mjs` fails on hex elsewhere in the package.
- Every surface colour has an `on-` partner for text (`--color-gx-primary` /
  `--color-gx-on-primary`). A theme overrides the whole set, not a single colour.
- Themes are `[data-gx-theme="<name>"]` blocks in `@layer base` and nest. The default (no
  attribute) is `arcade`.
- Z-index uses the scale (`--gx-z-hud`, `--gx-z-hud-raised`, `--gx-z-modal`, `--gx-z-toast`),
  never a bare number.
- Sizes that define the look (`--gx-px`, `--gx-depth`) are tokens; components never hard-code
  4px.
- Demo-only colours (sprite pixels drawn in code) may be literal.
